			"Message": "style(Output): Reorganize imports and fix indentation in Tauri main process service\n\nMove MistWebSocketTransport import after VSCode IPC type imports to follow logical grouping (external deps before internal modules). Remove extraneous blank line in tier resolution section. Fix inconsistent indentation on Node tier branch in TauriChannel.call().\n\nThese are purely cosmetic changes improving code readability in the Output component's Tauri main process entry point without altering runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "b21e8fd53e9fdf37a61517cd943e950a29038939"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T12:58:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1080,
				122
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): Add authoritative ESBuild configuration source modules\n\nAdd the complete ESBuild build system source to Configuration/ including: ESBuild entry configurations (Editor, VSCode, Bundle variants), exclusion rule modules (Bootstrap, Electron, Node, Network, Telemetry, Test, Types, WebWorker, Workbench, and Chromium IPC), plugin pipeline (Apply, Copy, Polyfill, Transform namespaces with 50+ transforms), runtime polyfills (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPC/Renderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcessProxy, Telemetry), and CEL services (ExposeAccessor, ExtensionsScanner, NullExtensionGallery, NullTelemetry, NullUpdate, Search, SharedProcess, DevLog, TauriMainProcess with MistWebSocketTransport, Trace). Also add TypeScript composite project configs for CodeEditorLand/Editor and Microsoft/VSCode targets.\n\nThese modules were previously only present as compiled .js/.js.map outputs in Configuration/ — the authoritative source now lives in the repository enabling reproducible builds, source-level debugging of the build pipeline, and version-controlled evolution of the Output component's bundling logic. The ESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via Compiler=Rest), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via Clean=true, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS Code's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility.",
			"SHA": "9c639bbef37f676169472c6845d926b9a7987ecf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T12:51:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				769,
